      "date": "2026-09-21 01:11:05.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good. The change is correct: `iflag=fullblock` makes dd loop on read() until a whole 20480-byte block is assembled, which is exactly what a `yes |` pipe cannot guarantee, and it matches the idiom already used in sanity-pfl.sh and sanity-flr.sh. One optional commit-message nit inline for whenever the patch is next refreshed - no need to re-spin for it.",
